<section class="panel rules-page"><% if(state) { %><a class="button button-gold" href="/game/tutorial">Tutorial</a><% } %><h1>Rules of the First Realm</h1><p>Kingdom Come is a multiplayer alpha inspired by Kingdoms Live. Our catalog and numerical rules are reconstructed, not recovered original server formulas.</p><h2>Quest, equip, invest</h2><p><% if(alpha.content.maxContentLevel>50) { %>Explore <%= alpha.content.areas.length %> regions with quests, equipment and Land through level <%= alpha.content.maxContentLevel %>. Classic equipment and legitimate owned items remain usable. The current XP transition keeps its original requirement; later transitions use the expanded progression curve. Combat reward formulas remain unchanged.<% } else { %>Explore eleven regions with quests and equipment through level 50, then work toward the Worldroot Bastion at level 55.<% } %> Mana runs repeatable quests. Equipment requirements stay owned; discoveries open later routes. Each army member automatically uses at most one weapon, one armor item and one spell; attack and defense choose different best items. Equipment sales return two-thirds of each copy’s recorded paid cost, rounded down. Land resale remains half its recorded paid cost.</p><h2>Resources and skills</h2><p>Health starts at 100, Mana at 20 and Stamina at 3. Recover 10 Health every 3 minutes, 1 Mana every 5 minutes and 1 Stamina every 2 minutes. Level-ups restore resources. One skill point adds 1 Mana or 10 Health; two add 1 Stamina. One point buys one Attack or Defense rating: +1% to the relevant army power, capped at 25 ratings each. Existing allocations remain unchanged. These training rules are reconstructed. Level milestones, ten quests and your first attacking victory award additional points.</p><h2>Land and upkeep</h2><p>All properties share one persistent 60-minute payment clock, including offline periods. Buying never shifts it. New holdings receive only their actual time to the next boundary, with sub-gold fractions carried forward. Subsequent complete hours pay the full saved rate. Earned partial time is also settled before a sale. Each additional property of the same type costs 10% more. Existing holdings keep their saved rates. All owned upkeep equipment accrues maintenance while funded. A reserve and carried gold pay it after due Land income; no passive income is required to buy equipment.</p><p>If funds run out, upkeep equipment pauses, free gear remains usable and further charges stop. Arrears never exceed one hourly bill at suspension. Earned income is credited once on the existing shared cycle. After accrued upkeep, carried gold and existing reserve credit automatically clear arrears and refill an affordable one-hour reserve. Remaining gold stays in your purse. A paused army can also resume when a quest or sale supplies enough carried gold. No Vault withdrawal, future-income advance or extra hourly payment is created. Manual Resume remains available and pays arrears plus one hour of reserve. No equipment is destroyed. Selling gear returns reserve above the new hourly bill; recorded arrears remain. The gold header forecasts the actual purse change at the next saved hourly payment. Open it for gross eligible earnings, property upkeep, active equipment costs, and any already prepaid reserve. Paused gear does not accrue new upkeep; affordable old arrears and reserve transfers appear separately. Purchases do not restart the clock.</p><h2>Rivals</h2><p>Attack uses 1 Stamina. The attacker needs 20 Health; the defender needs positive Health. Attack Again is available in your saved report immediately after each completed attack. A defeated, zero-Health opponent stays at 0 and recovers naturally before another attack. Ordinary victories and knockouts award neither Kills nor Deaths. Each completed bounty claim awards exactly one Kill to its claimant and one Death to its target. Similar-level rivals are eligible. Against human rivals, an attacking victory transfers 3% of the defender’s current unbanked gold, with no fixed per-victory gold maximum, before diminishing returns: 100%, 75%, 50%, 25%, then 10%. Each attacker–defender sequence resets exactly 24 hours after its first victory; defeats neither steal gold nor advance it. Each eligible human victory, attacking or defending, grants at least 1 XP. Passive NPCs keep their assigned levels. Defensive victories use a separate three-full-reward-victories-per-pair budget, then 1 XP. Defensive level-ups grant points without refilling combat resources or reviving a knocked-out target. Full XP starts at 5% of the <%= alpha.content.maxContentLevel>50?'legacy reward-base':'current' %> requirement through level 10, grows by 0.5 percentage points per level through 16, starts at 9% at 17, and grows by 0.375 points per level to 12% at 25 (base capped at 300). Relative levels scale this by 25%–150%, with 10 percentage points per opponent level. The actual opposing army strength scales XP up to 125%; an opponent below 35% of your relevant strength gives only 1 XP. Eligible non-trivial opponents scale between 50% and 125% of the base strength reward. Final XP rounds down with a minimum of 1. After three full-reward human encounters against a target, victories award 1 XP. Historical results keep their saved rules.</p><p>Temporary rivals never initiate attacks; their armies are capped at 10, equipment improves through level 50, and their Health recovers naturally. Bot encounters have no shared daily reward quota or one-win-per-rival cutoff. Bot ordinary gold uses 3% of the current unprotected purse, capped at 15,000 and min(3,000, 50 + floor(1.25 × target level²)), with target level capped at 50. The same-rival percentages are then 100%, 85%, 70%, 55%, and 40% for later victories in its existing fixed 24-hour sequence. Bot XP first uses 65% of the existing full difficulty award, rounded down with a minimum of 1. The same-rival percentage is then applied and rounded down, again keeping at least 1 XP per victory. Human and quest XP are unchanged. The 40% floor is provisional for alpha testing. Poor purses may yield no gold; much weaker opponents yield little XP. Losses and retries do not advance the victory sequence. Bot Land earns ordinary persistent income and bots prepay upkeep from their own purse at most once per saved income cycle. Attacks never trigger free wallet or upkeep refills.</p><h2>Your army</h2><p>You, accepted allies and retained militia share an active army limit that grows with level. <% if(alpha.content.maxContentLevel>50) { %>Capacity is the greater of five times your level and your legitimate retained army floor. Capacity never grants members; only you, retained militia and accepted allies participate. At level 100 the normal capacity is 500, with the same one-per-category equipment selection.<% } %> Existing militia stay owned. Gold cannot recruit new militia; expand through accepted allies. Quest army requirements are unchanged and can be reached by invitations. Each leader equips their own force. Calling specializations are modest: Barbarian has +4% attack, −2% defense and 10% shorter Stamina recovery intervals; Tank has +4% defense, −2% attack and 10% shorter Health intervals; Mage has −2% attack/defense and 10% shorter Mana intervals. First change is free; further changes cost 100 gold, at most once per 24 hours.</p><p>Recruit shows your persistent invitation code. An invitation changes neither army until its recipient accepts. You can reject or cancel pending invitations. Codes do not authenticate accounts; keep your password private. Distinct invitations have no daily quota or waiting period. A repeat invitation to the same player still requires 24 hours.</p><h2>Realm community</h2><p>Home offers All, Battles, Comments and Broadcasts. Profile comments are public and share the same records as the Home Comments feed. Comments allow <%= community.social.commentCharacters %> characters, one every <%= community.social.commentCooldownSeconds %> seconds, up to <%= community.social.commentsPerDay %> per rolling day. Broadcasts allow <%= community.social.broadcastCharacters %> characters, one every <%= community.social.broadcastCooldownSeconds %> seconds, up to <%= community.social.broadcastsPerDay %> per day; reach level 2 and finish three quests first.</p><p>Social posts give no gold or XP. Remove your own messages, hide unwanted comments on your profile or Report inappropriate content. Operators review reports and may hide messages or restrict posting. Hidden/deleted records remain for moderation audit. Public Profile → Battles shows paginated Tales From the Field; detailed reports and private snapshots stay restricted to combatants. Temporary rivals never post comments or broadcasts.</p><p>Health, Mana and Stamina recover automatically. The Vault protects deposited gold from attacks. Deposits and withdrawals have no fee and no interest. Only carried gold can fund purchases, upkeep or bounties; withdraw first. Tap Health to restore missing Health at missing Health × ceil(level / 10) gold. Free recovery settles first; full Health costs nothing. The server charges once and caps restoration at maximum Health. Settings provides account Sign Out; Profile retains your skills, inventory, property holdings and current income.</p><h2>Bounty List</h2><p>Fund an eligible rival’s bounty with carried gold plus a 10% fee. Place 1–10,000 gold after reviewing the exact fee (10%, rounded up, minimum 1 gold). Only an eligible finishing attacker who reduces the target to 0 Health claims escrow and one Kill; the target receives exactly one Death. Other knockouts count neither statistic. One active bounty per target; expiry after 24 hours; cancellation after one hour. Refunds return principal, not fees. Each target can receive at most 50 successful placements in a rolling 24 hours across all sponsors, including ended contracts. Relisting is immediate after a contract ends, subject to that shared limit. Eligible army allies of the sponsor or target may claim. Sponsors and targets cannot claim their own contracts. Temporary rivals never fund or claim bounties. They can be targets only when ENABLE_DEV_BOTS=1 and ENABLE_DEV_BOT_BOUNTIES=1 in development or an explicitly enabled Railway private alpha; ordinary production disables them. Bot bounty principal comes entirely from a real sponsor and does not reset the ordinary pair sequence. A sponsor needs a different eligible player identity to test the claim; their own funded contract is never claimable by them. <a href="/game/bounties">Read all limits on the Bounty List.</a></p><p>Active gameplay refinement: <strong><%= gameplay.id %></strong>. Other active rulesets: <strong><%= alpha.id %></strong>, <strong><%= strategy.id %></strong>, <strong><%= community.id %></strong>, <strong><%= refinements.id %></strong>, <strong><%= pvp.id %></strong>. Resources, purchases, sales, combat and payments are decided by the server.</p><a class="button button-outline" href="<%= state?'/game/home':'/login' %>">Return to realm</a></section>
